# Secure GPU Stack: RDMA device files for the video group only, like the GPU.
#
# On InfiniBand and RoCE machines, rdma-core's rules (and Mellanox OFED's)
# open the verbs and connection-manager devices to every local user, and
# Lambda Stack's A100 image had /dev/infiniband/uverbs0, rdma_cm and /dev/knem
# at 0666: any account, service or container could do RDMA, which skips the
# kernel's network stack, so neither the firewall nor strict outbound mode
# sees it. The people who run multi-node NCCL jobs are the ones who use the
# GPU, so they're in video already. ":=" stops later rules (rdma-core's are
# 90-) from opening them again. The management devices (umad, issm) are left
# root-only, as the kernel makes them: they send raw fabric management
# packets. Untested on InfiniBand hardware: no Lambda instance with it yet;
# single-GPU instances have no RDMA devices at all.
SUBSYSTEM=="infiniband_verbs", GROUP:="video", MODE:="0660"
KERNEL=="rdma_cm", GROUP:="video", MODE:="0660"
KERNEL=="knem", GROUP:="video", MODE:="0660"
KERNEL=="xpmem", GROUP:="video", MODE:="0660"
